{{also|stube}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|stube}}, from {{inh|de|goh|stuba}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*stubō||room, sitting room, oven}}, possibly from {{der|de|VL.|*extūfa}}, {{m|la|*extūfāre|t=to heat with steam}}, from {{der|de|la|ex-}} + {{m|la|*tūfus|t=hot vapor}}, from {{der|de|grc|τῦφος|t=fever}}.<ref>{{R:American_Heritage_Dictionary|stove}}</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|nds-de|[[Stuäwe]] (dative [[Stuäwe]], [[Stuäwen]], plural [[Stuäwen]]), [[Stuowe]] (dative [[Stuowen]]) {{q|Paderbornisch}}}}, {{cog|nl|stoof}}, {{cog|gmw-ecg||schduub}} {{q|Erzgebirgisch}}. See {{m|en|stove}} for more.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃtuːbə/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Stube.ogg|Audio}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|f|dim=^chen,^lein}}

# {{lb|de|regional}} [[living room]]
#: {{syn|de|Wohnzimmer}}
# [[room]] {{gloss|room used for a special purpose; the term is often found in compounds with somewhat old-fashioned character}}
# [[parlour]] {{gloss|a room used chiefly for representation purposes; often called {{m|de|gute Stube}} or the like}}
# the [[heated]] part of a traditional [[farmhouse]] (as opposed to stables, kitchen, etc.)
# {{lb|de|military}} [[bedroom]] in a [[barracks]]

